\title{lifeconformal: Conformal Prediction for Censored Life History Data}
\description{
Conformal calibration of prediction regions for state occupation times from censored multistate event histories. Fits working outcome and censoring models on training subjects and calibrates a fixed prediction score on independent subjects. Provides inverse-probability and augmented calibration, deterministic Markov reward calculations, history-dependent flexible transition models, and explicit numerical diagnostics.
}
\details{
The workflow separates score training and nuisance-model fitting from
calibration on an independent sample. The first version uses sample splitting;
cross-fitting is deferred. Use \code{\link[=LifeHist]{LifeHist()}} to describe observed histories,
\code{\link[=life_train]{life_train()}} to fit working models, \code{\link[=life_calibrate]{life_calibrate()}} on independent
subjects, and \code{\link[=predict]{predict()}} to obtain new baseline prediction regions.
Markov calculations use deterministic reward recursions. Flexible transition
models use frozen continuation streams and report their numerical settings.
}
